The Current Situation
Your updatePrediction controller probably ends like this:

await prediction.save();

res.redirect("/");
So regardless of whether you edited a prediction from:

Home

Premium

Yesterday's Results

you always end up back at:

/
The Solution (Production Approach)
Instead of making the controller guess where the user came from, let the form tell it.

Step 1 — Add a hidden field to homeForm.ejs
Inside your <form>:

<input
    type="hidden"
    name="redirectTo"
    value="<%= redirectTo || '/' %>"
>
Step 2 — Pass redirectTo from every Edit link
In home.ejs
Change:

<a href="/predictions/<%= prediction._id %>/edit">
to

<a href="/predictions/<%= prediction._id %>/edit?redirectTo=/">
In premium.ejs
Change to

<a href="/predictions/<%= prediction._id %>/edit?redirectTo=/predictions/premium">
In yesterday.ejs
Change to

<a href="/predictions/<%= prediction._id %>/edit?redirectTo=/predictions/yesterdaysresults">
Step 3 — Update editPrediction
Instead of just rendering the form:

res.render("predictions/homeForm", {
    prediction
});
render:

res.render("predictions/homeForm", {
    prediction,
    redirectTo: req.query.redirectTo || "/"
});
Now the form remembers where it came from.

Step 4 — Update updatePrediction
Near the top:

const { redirectTo } = req.body;
Then after saving:

await prediction.save();

res.redirect(redirectTo || "/");
That's it.

The Result
If the admin edits from Home:

Home
 ↓
Edit
 ↓
Save
 ↓
Home ✅
If editing from Premium:

Premium
 ↓
Edit
 ↓
Save
 ↓
Premium ✅
If editing from Yesterday's Results:

Yesterday's Results
 ↓
Edit
 ↓
Save
 ↓
Yesterday's Results ✅
No if...else, no checking isPremium, no checking status.

Why I prefer this
I actually prefer this approach over writing something like:

if (prediction.isPremium) {
    ...
}

if (prediction.status === "Won") {
    ...
}
because the controller doesn't need to know why you're editing—it simply returns you to wherever you came from. That's cleaner, more flexible, and easier to extend. If you later add pages like /predictions/expired or /predictions/pending, the redirect logic still works without any controller changes.

