The fact that it's correct in the database but wrong on the Premium page tells me the issue is probably not this code. Instead, it's likely one of these:

Possibility 1 (Most likely): The date is being stored with a timezone shift
When you submit a datetime-local input like:

<input type="datetime-local" name="kickoffTime">
the browser sends:

2026-07-18T20:00
Notice there's no timezone attached.

JavaScript interprets that in the server's local timezone, while MongoDB stores dates in UTC. Depending on your environment (especially on Render vs. your local machine), you can end up with a one-hour difference.

Possibility 2: The value is changing during the update
