I know exactly where to look.
In predictions.ejs you have:

value="<%= prediction ? new Date(prediction.kickoffTime).toISOString().slice(0,16) : '' %>"
toISOString() is the culprit.

It always converts the date to UTC.

Example:

MongoDB
19:00 Lagos

↓

UTC

18:00Z

↓

toISOString()

2026-07-18T18:00
Then your browser displays

18:00
instead of

19:00
When you click Update, you save the wrong time back into MongoDB.

Every edit shifts it another hour.

This is the real bug.
Don't use

toISOString()
for <input type="datetime-local">.

