The fix is only about 5–6 lines, and after that:

✅ Home page will display correctly.

✅ Premium page will display correctly.

✅ Yesterday page will display correctly.

✅ Editing a prediction will no longer subtract one hour every time you save.

I think we've finally located the root cause of the kickoff time bug.



            <input 
            class="form-control mb-3" 
            type="datetime-local" 
            name="kickoffTime"
            value="<%= prediction ? new Date(prediction.kickoffTime).toISOString().slice(0,16) : '' %>"
            >

Perfect. This is the line causing the entire problem. 🎯

value="<%= prediction ? new Date(prediction.kickoffTime).toISOString().slice(0,16) : '' %>"
toISOString() always converts the date to UTC, which is why you're losing one hour every time you edit a prediction.

The correct solution
Replace that entire value attribute with this:

value="<%= prediction
    ? new Date(new Date(prediction.kickoffTime).getTime() - new Date(prediction.kickoffTime).getTimezoneOffset() * 60000)
        .toISOString()
        .slice(0,16)
    : '' %>"
Why this works
Suppose MongoDB stores:

2026-07-18T18:00:00.000Z
which is actually:

19:00 Africa/Lagos
The code:

new Date(prediction.kickoffTime).getTimezoneOffset()
calculates your timezone difference.

Then:

getTime() - offset
moves the time back into your local timezone before calling toISOString().

The browser finally receives:

2026-07-18T19:00
instead of

2026-07-18T18:00
